Rankings of individuals by genetic values estimated from each a single year of data significantly differed from the multi-year genetic rankings in Spearman rank correlation tests ( p < 0.001, Additional file 2 ). Rank correlations between the 2010-derived predictions and the multi-year predictions were lower than the subsequent years (2010: 0.35–0.63; 2011: 0.58–0.92; 2012: 0.85–0.97). However, correlations between breeding values estimated from a single year and their respective phenotypes implied a better fit within a year for each year and trait than the single-year breeding values with their multi-year counterparts ( ρ = 0.64–1.00) (Additional file 2 ).
